  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through its partnership with DFAT, CBM Australia (CBM) provides capacity support to the Pacific Disability Forum (PDF). PDF is the regional organisation of people with disability and a key partner for the Australian development program. This ongoing collaboration with CBM has helped PDF expand its influence and reach in promoting disability equity and rights. For example, CBM supported PDF&#x2019;s thought leadership on the need for systems-level change and a refocus from disability inclusion to disability equity and rights. PDF&#x2019;s articulation of these priorities shaped Australia&#x2019;s International Disability Equity and Rights Strategy. CBM has also helped grow PDF&#x2019;s capacity to service a diverse and growing list of member organisations across the Pacific. 
&#x200d;
Central to the success of the CBM - PDF relationship is mutual trust and respect, a long-term commitment and a principle of being &#x2018;on tap but not on top&#x2019;. CBM provides peer-to-peer support, coaches team members to deliver on PDF&#x2019;s organisational objectives and offers technical input. In doing so it focusses on strengthening team capacity, communication and prioritising PDF&#x2019;s agenda. This approach is flexible and responsive to the needs of both individual staff and PDF as a whole.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
